// Firestore security rules for redeem codes (main.js redeemSecretCode reads codes/{CODE}).
//
// HOW CODES WORK: each code is one document in the "codes" collection, and the document id is the code in UPPER CASE.
// Add, edit or delete them in the Firebase console (Firestore Database > codes) and players see the change straight away,
// with no redeploy. Fields:
//   type       string   'count' (What Happeneds), 'golden' (Golden), or 'diamonds' (gems)       required
//   amount     number   how many (for 'count' you can also use a string such as '1e100')      required
//   message    string   shown to the player when they redeem it                                  optional
//   enabled    boolean  set to false to switch a code off without deleting it                    optional
//   expiresAt  timestamp the code stops working after this time                                  optional
// Example: document id GEMS -> { type: 'diamonds', amount: 100, message: 'You received 100 gems!' }
//
// HOW TO USE THE RULES: copy the `match /codes/{code}` block into your existing rules (Firebase console > Firestore
// Database > Rules), inside `match /databases/{database}/documents { ... }`, then Publish. Don't replace your whole rules
// with this file: your clan, chat, leaderboard and saves collections need their own rules.
//
// IMPORTANT: Firestore allows a request if ANY matching rule allows it. If your rules contain a catch-all such as
//     match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if true; }
// then anyone can read the whole codes collection and also create or change codes (including ones that give a huge
// reward). Remove the catch-all and write rules for each collection you use.
//
// `get` (read one document by id) is allowed, `list` (browse the collection) is not, so a player can only check a code
// they already know. Writes are denied to every client; only you, in the console, can change codes.

rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /codes/{code} {
      allow get: if true;
      allow list, create, update, delete: if false;
    }
  }
}
